# Release archive contents
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# spec-kit's catalog installs this extension from GitHub's generated tag ZIP
# (https://github.com/WangX0111/superspec/archive/refs/tags/vX.Y.Z.zip). That
# archive is produced by `git archive`, which honours `export-ignore`, so every
# path marked below is present in the repository (and for `--dev` installs) but
# is stripped from the published archive.
#
# This matters because spec-kit validates archives before extracting them
# (src/specify_cli/_download_security.py):
#
#   MAX_DOWNLOAD_BYTES     50 MiB   whole archive as downloaded
#   MAX_ZIP_ENTRIES           512   number of members
#   MAX_ZIP_MEMBER_BYTES   10 MiB   single uncompressed member
#   MAX_ZIP_TOTAL_BYTES    50 MiB   sum of uncompressed members
#
# assets/workflow-overview-en.png alone is ~12 MiB, which tripped the per-member
# limit and made `specify extension add superspec` fail (issue #6).
#
# Keep this list in sync with scripts/validate-release-archive.py, which fails
# CI if the archive regains excluded paths, loses runtime files, or approaches
# any of the limits above.

# Documentation media — rendered from the repository on GitHub, never read at
# runtime. This is the payload that broke catalog installs.
assets/            export-ignore

# Sample project and real-run snapshots — teaching material for readers of the
# repository, not part of the installed extension.
examples/          export-ignore

# Development, validation and end-to-end test tooling.
scripts/           export-ignore
.github/           export-ignore

# Git metadata that has no meaning inside an installed extension directory.
.gitattributes     export-ignore
.gitignore         export-ignore

# Secondary translation of the README; README.md ships as the required doc.
README_zh.md       export-ignore
